Why do systems that work in normal conditions fail under stress?
Answer:
Systems that perform well under normal conditions often fail under stress because normal conditions hide edge cases. Stress introduces time pressure, incomplete information, overload, and human error simultaneously.
Without explicit design for these conditions, assumptions break silently until collapse occurs. Experts assume stress will happen and design accordingly.

